<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI24-MINOR-108>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI24-MINOR-108" ;
  triage:title "Same-peer double-dispatch still serializes across full I/O window on per-peer PeerSyncProgress lock" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs sync_peer() (lines ~683-711) holds the per-peer Arc[Mutex[PeerSyncProgress]] guard across the full blocking reconcile_peer I/O (up to 5s) for the SAME peer, so two concurrent explicit sync_peer calls for one peer still serialize rather than the second fast-failing via next_allowed_at cooldown check. Cross-peer stalling (the original AI24-IMPORTANT-002 defect) is fixed; this same-peer double-dispatch latency is a smaller-blast-radius residual noted by rust-service-hardening-agent, flagged for an explicit accept/fix decision, not a regression of the closed finding."^^xsd:string ;
